  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nWith a couple minor exceptions, little change in the weather\npattern is expected until late next week. An upper level\ndisturbance may result in a few showers in the northwest part of\nour forecast area Monday night into Tuesday, and a second\ndisturbance may result in a few more showers Thursday night into\nFriday. Otherwise, well above normal temperatures will continue\nthrough next week, especially for daytime highs. With low dew\npoints continuing, lowered nighttime lows below the NBM the next \nfew nights, especially in the normally colder spots.\n\nThe next chance for significant rainfall looks to come around next\nweekend, and we may finally get a decent cold front in here right\naround the first of November, but we will just have to wait and \nsee on that.",
